why: Kirill could not follow a note that said an old platform call refuses a type naming its parts; a platform fact is the event a reader can watch, so the note says what the call answers when the two are asked about together, and the act follows from that event
labelled: 2026-09-30
--- code
export function schemeQueryKind(entryType: string): string {
  return entryType.split(';')[0];
}
--- facts
On the oldest clearing hosts, `canPost` answers that a posting cannot settle when an entry type that names its currencies and a settlement scheme are asked about together.
The scheme is asked about the posting kind alone, without the currencies.
